Events
Click on Groups & Settings > All Settings > Admin > Events.
Each event has three, filterable, primary characteristics: Type, Severity, and Category
Type has two options: Console and Device
Severity has eight options in descending order of criticality: (0) Emergency, (1) Alert, (2) Critical, (3) Error, (4) Warning, (5) Notice, (6) Information, and (7) Debug
Category has too many options to list.
Examples
For examples of event data available, the following can be done:
From within their AirWatch console, click on Hub > Reports & Analytics > Events > Device Events or Hub > Reports & Analytics > Events > Console Events
Click on the event data column to see the information that would get sent over to the syslog server for a given event.
Facilities
Used on the syslog server side for filtering events.
See explanation - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syslog
Scheduler Service
The scheduler service sends all syslog events, Device and Console events, settings should reflect the selection for both in the syslog settings (Groups & Settings > All Settings > System > Enterprise Integration > Syslog).
